# `std/parsing/regex` against the reference it replaces — conformance test

`PRegex` used to be answered by the **host**: `java.util.regex` reached through a native string
method, so each lane got its own engine's dialect. `std/parsing/regex.ssc` answers it in
ScalaScript instead, and the reason this case declares four backends is the whole argument for
that change — the same program, the same answers, everywhere.

Every expectation below was **produced by** `java.util.regex.Pattern.lookingAt()` rather than
written by hand, so a disagreement here is a real behaviour change and not a taste dispute.

Three blocks, and the third exists because a negative control demanded it. Patching the matcher to
take the longest greedy run and never hand characters back left blocks 1 and 2 **fully green** —
the module's hardest path was untested until these ten cases were added. Two other controls are on
record: defining `$` as plain `pos == length` reddens 2 cases, and dropping the zero-width guard
sends the matcher into unbounded recursion.

## Imports

[regexMatchPrefix](std/parsing/regex.ssc)

## The harness

```scalascript
// Render a matched string so a newline or tab is visible in a failure line.
def rxEsc(s: String): String =
  var out = ""
  var i = 0
  while i < s.length do
    val c = s.charAt(i).toInt
    if c == 10 then out = out + "\\n"
    else if c == 9 then out = out + "\\t"
    else if c == 13 then out = out + "\\r"
    else out = out + s.drop(i).take(1)
    i = i + 1
  out

// `Option[String]`, not `Any`. With an `Any` parameter `case Some(m)` binds m as Any, and the
// JVM lane — which compiles this file as real Scala — rejects `rxEsc(m)` on the spot.
def rxShow(r: Option[String]): String =
  r match
    case Some(m) => "Some(" + rxEsc(m) + ")"
    case other => "None"

def chk(pat: String, in: String, want: String): Int =
  val got = rxShow(regexMatchPrefix(in, pat))
  if got == want then 0
  else
    println("FAIL /" + pat + "/ @ " + rxEsc(in) + " -> " + got + " want " + want)
    1

var bad = 0
bad = bad + chk("$", "", "Some()")
bad = bad + chk("$", "abc", "None")
bad = bad + chk("$", "\n", "Some()")
bad = bad + chk("$", "abc\n", "None")
bad = bad + chk("$", "abc\\r\n", "None")
bad = bad + chk("$", "\n\n", "None")
bad = bad + chk("([ \\t]*\\n)*", "", "Some()")
bad = bad + chk("([ \\t]*\\n)*", "\n", "Some(\\n)")
bad = bad + chk("([ \\t]*\\n)*", "  \n\t\nx", "Some(  \\n\\t\\n)")
bad = bad + chk("([ \\t]*\\n)*", "   x", "Some()")
bad = bad + chk("([ \\t]*\\n)*", "\n\n\n", "Some(\\n\\n\\n)")
bad = bad + chk("-?[0-9]+", "42", "Some(42)")
